<!--
  Ship UI landing — kinetic direction (designer option 1c), with a static
  batteries-included headline. Loops the language deliberately lacks
  (marquee, wordmark gradient) live in base.css with reduced-motion guards.
-->
<column class="landing-wrap">
  <column class="hero kinetic-hero" gap="4">
    <center><p class="eyebrow">SHIP UI · 0.2.0</p></center>
    <h1>
      <strong class="rotator-slot">
        {#for w of word() key={w}}
          <b class="rotator" motion:enter={{ opacity: 'fade' }}>{w}</b>
        {/for}
      </strong>
      included.<br /><b class="accent">Actually.</b>
    </h1>
    <center>
      <p class="lead">
        One language with the whole interface inside it — built for agents to
        write and humans to review, with no way to drift off the design system.
      </p>
    </center>
    <row class="hero-cta" gap="2">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/getting-started" motion:press={{ scale: 'press' }}>Get started</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/why">Why a language?</a>
    </row>
  </column>
</column>

<column class="marquee-band">
  <row class="track" gap="0">
    <p>NO RAW CSS ◆ SIGNALS BUILT IN ◆ 48 COMPONENTS ◆ 9 THEMES ◆ A11Y BY CONSTRUCTION ◆ NO RAW CSS ◆ SIGNALS BUILT IN ◆ 48 COMPONENTS ◆ 9 THEMES ◆ A11Y BY CONSTRUCTION ◆ NO RAW CSS ◆ SIGNALS BUILT IN ◆ 48 COMPONENTS ◆ 9 THEMES ◆ A11Y BY CONSTRUCTION ◆ NO RAW CSS ◆ SIGNALS BUILT IN ◆ 48 COMPONENTS ◆ 9 THEMES ◆ A11Y BY CONSTRUCTION ◆&nbsp;</p>
  </row>
</column>
<column class="marquee-band alt">
  <row class="track" gap="0">
    <p>forms + validation · live data · springs + tweens · ssr · hot reload · design tokens · forms + validation · live data · springs + tweens · ssr · hot reload · design tokens · forms + validation · live data · springs + tweens · ssr · hot reload · design tokens · forms + validation · live data · springs + tweens · ssr · hot reload · design tokens ·&nbsp;</p>
  </row>
</column>

<column class="landing-wrap">
  <column gap="3" sx="py:8">
    <center><h2>Nine themes. One attribute.</h2></center>
    <center>
      <p sx="fg:muted-foreground max-w:panel-max-w-md">
        Components read tokens, never colors — so a theme is a complete
        aesthetic, applied in one move. Don't take the word for it; this site
        runs on it.
      </p>
    </center>
    <center>
      <button on:click={openThemes} variant="solid" tone="primary" motion:press={{ scale: 'press' }}>
        Open the theme picker
      </button>
    </center>
  </column>

  <column class="products" gap="3">
    <a class="product-card" href="/overview">
      <h3>SUI <small class="tag">framework</small></h3>
      <p>Components, layout, styling, theming, animation and state. Write a page in markup; the framework already has the rest.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="product-card" href="/components">
      <h3>Components <small class="tag">48, included</small></h3>
      <p>Buttons, dialogs, combobox, tabs, tables, toasts — accessible, keyboard-complete, and themed. Nothing to install.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="product-card" href="/deck">
      <h3>Deck <small class="tag">app framework</small></h3>
      <p>Routing, server rendering, bundling, live data, and a hot-reloading dev loop. The application layer.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="product-card" href="/ai">
      <h3>AI <small class="tag">agent tooling</small></h3>
      <p>Built to be written by agents: the compiler is the guardrail, plus MCP tooling and a scored authoring eval.</p>
    </a>
  </column>

  <p class="wordmark" motion:view={{ opacity: 'fade', translate-y: 'spring:deliberate' }}>SHIP</p>
</column>
